WEBVTT

00:09:57.885 --> 00:10:03.724
And this is how the "Tribune" writes
about the atmosphere in game five, 1932:

00:10:05.100 --> 00:10:09.146
"The cash customers fanned to fever heat
by the ardor and closeness of combat

00:10:09.146 --> 00:10:12.441
gave outlet to all kinds
of riotous impulses."

00:10:12.441 --> 00:10:13.692
Alright?

00:10:13.734 --> 00:10:17.321
This may not sound familiar yet,
but our girl, Ada Anderson?

00:10:17.363 --> 00:10:21.241
1879, the "New York Times"
writes about her walk.

00:10:21.241 --> 00:10:22.493
Her walk.

00:10:22.493 --> 00:10:25.371
"Many women were seen to faint
in the dense crowd,

00:10:25.412 --> 00:10:27.247
but as they could not be carried out,

00:10:27.247 --> 00:10:29.875
it is not known what became of them."

00:10:29.917 --> 00:10:32.878
(Laughter)